Column names are resolved case-insensitively from a table of aliases, so
\code{Sender}/\code{Receiver}, \code{source}/\code{target} and \code{onset}/\code{terminus} are all
understood without being spelled out. Times may be numeric, \code{Date},
\code{POSIXct} or character date-time strings; character and date-time input is
converted to elapsed time since the first event in a readable unit.

Vertices are addressed by name everywhere in this package. Integer vertex
